  "description": "Avg Gain of 16.4%… Here’s What the BIG Winners All Had in Common",
  "body_html": "<p>If you like stocks, <strong>watch this video if you have 12 minutes of free time</strong>. If not, save it and watch it when you can pay attention, its a denser post. </p><p>If you are not familiar with the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-summary?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Screener</a>, this is a Python script that I built, and algorithmically scans over 5000 stocks everyday at market close, for an expansive set of requirements. It targets the strongest trending stocks, with high volume pivot breakouts. Many of the requirements are derived from Mark Minervini, two-time U.S. investing champion and Trend Following, by Michael Covel. </p><p>Assuming you bought every single stock the screener signaled, all 545 of them since July, and held all of them to today (12/4), your win/loss numbers would look something like this:</p><ul><li><p>Total Net Sum: 8950% - winners win big…its accumulative…no, I have not achieved this percent in my own portfolio lol. This is for context.</p></li><li><p>Average % PnL for all stocks:  16.42%</p></li><li><p>Win Percentage: 60.5% </p></li></ul><p>Obviously…we cannot buy every single stock. We verified that the StockTok Screener had a winning track record back in May 2025 and July 2025. It was reviewed externally from me as well, to prevent cherry picked data. You are welcome to review those analysis here: <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-screener-results-2-weeks?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Screener Review May 2025</a>, <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/77-days-in-how-the-stocktok-screener?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Screner Review July 2025</a>. <strong>The point of this paragraph: it continues to bat a high winning percentage, and chooses some huge running stocks. </strong>We want to continue to see win percentages over 50%, which we are well above and want average % PnL to be substantial…indicating most stocks do in fact run upwards. Achieved! <strong>✅  </strong></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><h4>Top 10 Best Performers (from signal to 12/4):</h4><ol><li><p>Bloom Energy, BE:                      230%     7/25/2025</p></li><li><p>Lumentum Holdings, LITE:      175%     8/9/2025</p></li><li><p>Cipher Mining, CIFR:                 155%    8/30/2025</p></li><li><p>Cidara Therapeutics, CDTX:     131%    9/30/2025</p></li><li><p>Applied Digital, APLD:              130%    7/31/2025</p></li><li><p>Iren Limited, IREN:                    106%    8/24/2025</p></li><li><p>Applovin Corp, APP:                   75%     8/1/2025</p></li><li><p>Indivior PLC, INDV:                    74%     7/31/2025</p></li><li><p>Hut 8 Corp., HUT                         74%     8/15/2025</p></li><li><p>Ciena Corp., CIEN                       68%     9/5/2025</p></li></ol><p>I had to standardize how stocks were evaluated for fairness, so all were measure from signal date to present day. For example, Bloom Energy actually peaked at 342% gain, but today it sits at 230% gain. </p><p>But this is information we already know. What I wanted to do now, was evaluate what were the common traits of the BEST runners? What were those days like? How was the stock behaving? What was the VIX doing? <strong>I</strong> <strong>only evaluated stocks greater than 30% </strong>gain from time of initial signal. </p><ul><li><p>Other stocks had tremendous performance as well, but experienced declines in stock price <em><strong>after </strong></em>large run ups. Some of these were still positive, some were negative. Just narrowed down the list for easier and more longer term analysis.</p></li></ul><h4>Common Traits of Top Performers at Signal:</h4><ul><li><p>The VIX was always below 21, 100% of the time. The VIX between 14.8 to 16.7 was optimal investing time. I will be adjusting my investing rule of VIX less than 22 to VIX less than 21 because of this. I may tighten even more or include a rule of: If VIX 20 day MA is pointing up, turn off screener…though I still need to see how effective this is over time. Just a thought.</p></li><li><p>Every single stock was above the 10, 20 and 50 day moving average at time of signal. All of them.</p></li><li><p>Every single stock was within -25% of their 52-week high. 61% of the stocks were presently breaking their 52-week high. </p></li><li><p>66% of the time, the stock gapped up at signal. Point: don’t be scared of pump ups, these are good signals. </p></li><li><p>Nearly ALL of the stocks had long, well established uptrends. To measure this, I utilized my <a href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/script/YkJaCmZq-StockTok-Trend-Indicator/\">StockTok Trend Indicator</a> (help yourself! Click link, add to favorites, then just add to your chart!) and measured the days between when the StockTok screener gave a signal to when the indicator produced a signal. Results were kind of surprising:</p><ul><li><p>On average, the stock had already been trending up for 71 days. </p></li><li><p>69% of the time, the stock had been trending up for more than a month.</p><ul><li><p>The point of this: Don’t think a stock is near a top; most of them had been trending up for months…and continued trending up for months. </p><p></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/screener-continues-to-find-monster/comments&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Leave a comment&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/screener-continues-to-find-monster/comments\"><span>Leave a comment</span></a></p></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><p>Now, the screener does have rules about total shares outstanding, but I will be refining those rules a bit more. In short, stocks with less than ~400M, generally, performed much better. Stocks greater than ~400M, generally, were underperformers. The “perfect” number is stocks under 262M…but I don’t want to constrain ourselves too much.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png\" width=\"1143\" height=\"604\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:604,&quot;width&quot;:1143,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:140726,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/180710466?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Q6iL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb4c79c02-e2a6-4264-a95a-afdbce8f89c2_1143x604.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Of course there are exceptions, but most winning stocks had less than 400M total shares outstanding.</figcaption></figure></div><p> Another interesting observation, was the market cap size of the winners at time of signal. Now, this cannot be a hard rule, but something to consider:</p><ul><li><p>Most of the winners had a market cap between $5B and $18B, with an average of $18.7B. </p></li><li><p>Most of the losers had a much higher market cap already, with an average of $35.3B.</p></li></ul><p>What use is this information? Ignore the stocks that pop on the screener with say, $2B market cap. Most of the winning stocks are between $4.5B and $18B. I will do between $4B and $19B for simplicity. That is not to say you can’t get a loser in that market cap range, but at least we are in the sweet spot for potential.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Lf-T!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Lf-T!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Lf-T!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Lf-T!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Lf-T!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Lf-T!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png\" width=\"552\" height=\"620\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/86b828d6-1a80-4b2b-9349-9735bd49a0ac_552x620.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:620,&quot;width&quot;:552,&quot;resizeWi